Well, all three of my attempts to reply to the "Why bless?" question via
email have bounced, so I'm just going to post my response.  Spoilers ahead,
and no guarantees that my quotes or my information are correct.

Spoilers!

I hear blessed weapons hit more often when you're fighting undead.
I think they resist rusting a little better, too.  (as does blessed armor)
I hear blessed bags of holding weigh less than their uncursed counterparts.

A blessed magic lamp (if not yet used) should always give you a Wish when you
#rub it to free the djinni inside.

A blessed unicorn horn, if Applied, will cure poison, sickness, confusion,
stun, and sometimes restore abilities.  You can also dip them into potions
that cause these negative effects, and turn them into water. (handy for
making holy water)

However, the real advantage in blessing stuff is with Potions and Scrolls.

For example, potions of invisibility....
CURSED
	"Somehow, you feel your presence is known."
UNCURSED
	(normal)
BLESSED
	"Would you like the invisibility to be permanent? [yn]"


Potions of Gain Level...
CURSED
	"You rise up, through the ceiling!"
UNCURSED
	(normal)
BLESSED
	(puts you about half-way to the *next* level as well)


Scrolls of Enchant Armor/Weapon can potentially enchant by as much as +3
(instead of just +1) when blessed.

Blessed Scrolls of Remove Curse affect every item in your inventory.
(Cursed ones sometimes curse items you're carrying.)

Blessed Scrolls of Genocide affect all monster represented by a given symbol.
Uncursed Scrolls of Genocide affect all monsters with a specific name.
Cursed Scrolls of Genocide *SUMMON* several of the specified monster.

Cursed Scrolls of Teleportation will Level Teleport you.
(If you have Teleport Control, they'll ask you what level you want.)

Cursed Scrolls of Confuse Monster will confuse *you*.
Uncursed ones affect the next monster you hit.
Blessed ones affect the next several monsters you hit.

Scare Monster scrolls are good once if cursed, twice if uncursed, thrice
if blessed.  (They downgrade one level when you pick them up, if they're
already cursed, they crumble to dust in your hands.)

Blessed Spellbooks are *always* successfully read/learned.
Cursed ones usually screw you up pretty badly.

If you have any other specific examples you'd like to know about, ask me and
I might know the answer.  (If you can supply an email address that I can
actually reach.  :-) )

